                </l>
                <seg xml:id="seg_c_1">c</seg>
                <l> Nunc et incomptis <name key="Curius">Curium</name> capillis <seg
                        type="translation" xml:lang="en">Him, and Curius with his uncombed
                        hair,</seg>
                </l>
                <seg xml:id="seg_u_1">u</seg>
                <l> Utilem bello tulit et Camillum <seg type="translation" xml:lang="en">and <name
                            key="Camillus">Camillus</name>, to be useful in war, </seg>
                </l>
                <l>
                    <choice>
                        <abbr>Saēua</abbr>
                        <expan>Saeva</expan>
                    </choice> paupertas et <choice>
                        <abbr>auitꝰ</abbr>
                        <expan>avitus</expan>
                    </choice> apto cum lare fundus. <seg type="translation" xml:lang="en">cruel
                        poverty bred, along with an ancestral farm and a fitting home.</seg>
                </l>
                <l> Crescit occulto <choice>
                        <abbr>uelut</abbr>
                        <expan>velut</expan>
                    </choice> arbor <choice>
                        <abbr>aeuo</abbr>
                        <expan>aevo</expan>
                    </choice>
                    <seg type="translation" xml:lang="en">Like a tree in the unperceived passing of
                        time grows </seg>
                </l>
                <seg xml:id="seg_Ø_2">Ø</seg>
                <l> Fama <name key="Marcellus">Marcelli</name> micat inter <choice>
                        <abbr>omnis</abbr>
                        <expan>omnes</expan>
                    </choice>
                    <seg type="translation" xml:lang="en">the fame of Marcellus.</seg>
                </l>
                <note type="addition">l</note>
                <l> Iulium sidus <choice>
                        <abbr>uelut</abbr>
                        <expan>velut</expan>
                    </choice> inter ignes luna minores <seg type="translation" xml:lang="en">The
                        julian star shines among them all like the moon among the lesser
                        fires.</seg>
                </l>
                <l> Gentis humanae pater atque custos <seg type="translation" xml:lang="en">Father
                        and guardian of the human race,</seg>
                </l>
                <l>
                    <name key="orte Saturno">Orte Saturno</name> tibi cura magni <seg
                        type="translation" xml:lang="en">son of Saturn, the care of great</seg>
                </l>
                <l>
                    <name key="Caesar">Caesaris</name> fatis data, tu secundo Caesare regnes <seg
                        type="translation" xml:lang="en">Caesar has been given to you by the fates,
                        may you reign with Caesar second only to you. </seg>
                </l>
                <l> Ille seu <name key="Parthians">Parthos</name>
                    <name key="Latium">Latio</name> imminentes <seg type="translation" xml:lang="en"
                        >Whether the Parthians who now overhang Latium,</seg>
                </l>
                <note target="#Egerit_1" type="synonym">subegerit</note>
                <l>
                    <seg xml:id="seg_Egerit_1">Egerit</seg> iusto domitos triumpho <seg
